WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.280
- Hello and welcome everybody.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.720
It's really good to have
you here with us today.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.610
I'm Kim Goff-Crews, I am the
Secretary and Vice President

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:15.550
for University Life here at Yale.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.410
And I'm the University Officer
who leads Belonging at Yale,

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.860
which is the university's
activity's actual initiative,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.360
which is designed to enhance
diversity, support equity,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.160
and also promote a sense of wellbeing,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.540
a sense of inclusion and
belonging and welcome

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.990
for all of our community members.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:34.760
Now today's conversation is one

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.070
of a series of occasional
conversations that we have

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.250
sponsored by Belonging at Yale.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.648
Some of you I know have been with us

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:47.648
in our conversations with
Dolly Chugh or with Ibram Kendi.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.588
Others of you might have joined

00:00:49.588 --> 00:00:52.800
the first My Story event that
we had a couple of weeks ago,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.440
where we feature students,
faculty, staff, and alumni,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.270
to talk about their sense
of belonging on campus,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.500
so really interesting event.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.430
So whether you've been with me before

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.710
on some of these other events,
or this is your first time,

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.850
a hearty welcome to you today.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.090
I do wanna point out that
the Belonging at Yale website

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:13.340
features a lot of calendar,
which have a lot of these events

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.500
and some of the taping
of some of the events.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.550
So I ask you to check that
out regularly as well.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.994
But today our conversation is
gonna be really interesting

00:01:20.994 --> 00:01:23.720
and very timely and on point.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.920
Respecting all Connecticut families,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.640
the legal parent-child
relationship for unmarried,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.900
same sex and non-biological parents.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.000
This is a topic that's actually
interesting for everybody.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.650
But I'm particularly
glad to host this event

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:41.623
this month in April, when
we celebrate LGBTQ PRIDE.

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.210
In conversation today,

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.530
our two of our Yale community members,

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.330
a faculty and staff member.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.410
Douglas NeJaime who teaches
at the Yale Law School

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:52.243
is with us.

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:55.050
He is the Anne Urowsky Professor of Law,

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.670
and he has a secondary
appointment by the way,

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.180
at the Yale Child Study Center.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.297
Doug teaches courses on
professional responsibility,

00:02:02.297 --> 00:02:05.110
family law, the
constitution of both family

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.590
and also law and sexuality.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.910
But he is for today's
purposes, the principal drafter

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:12.920
of the Connecticut Parentage Act.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.240
That act for those of you don't know,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.160
passed with near unanimous support,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.498
which is hard to do nowadays,
so really well done, Doug,

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:23.100
near unanimous support from
Connecticut legislators

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.523
and it was signed into law
by the Governor in 2021.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.480
He is going to be in conversation
with Deb Stanley-McAulay

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.380
who is the Associate Vice President

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.520
for Employee Engagement
and Workplace Culture.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.470
Many of us know that Deb

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.900
